[Chapter "Against ...g6"]
[Line "The h-pawn attack"]
[Opening "Rapport-Jobava System"]

{Against a kingside fianchetto, White attacks it with the h-pawn.} 1. d4 {Start with the queen's pawn.} 1... d5 2. Nc3 {The Jobava idea: the knight comes to c3 before the c-pawn moves, ready for Nb5 or e4.} 2... Nf6 3. Bf4 {Develop the bishop outside the pawn chain before e3.} 3... g6 {Black fianchettoes.} 4. e3 {Solid base first.} 4... Bg7 5. h4 {The standard plan against ...g6: march the h-pawn to open the h-file.} 5... O-O 6. h5 {Black has castled into the attack. White will open the h-file with hxg6.} *
